## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: vì sao không nên test chi tiết triển khai.**

> *"The rule I follow is: test what the user experiences, not how the component is built.*
> *If I write a test that checks internal state, or how many times a hook was called, that test is tied to my implementation. The moment I refactor — even if the app behaves exactly the same — the test goes red. So it costs me time without catching a real bug. That's a brittle test.*
> *Instead I query the way a user would. Find the button by its accessible name, press it, and assert on what appears on screen. If I rewrite the internals but the screen still behaves correctly, the test should stay green — because nothing the user cares about changed.*
> *There's a nice side effect too. Querying by accessible label pushes you to actually add accessibility labels, so your app gets more usable for screen readers as a by-product of writing good tests.*
> *The boundary is that this style is slower than pure unit tests, so I don't do it for everything. Business logic goes in pure functions with plain unit tests, and I save component tests for the parts with real interaction — mostly forms."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `go red` / `stay green` | test hỏng / test đậu | *The test goes red after a refactor.* |
| `tied to` | bị buộc chặt vào | *That test is tied to my implementation.* |
| `side effect` (n) | tác dụng phụ (ở đây là tốt) | *There's a nice side effect too.* |
| `by-product` (n) | sản phẩm đi kèm | *Accessibility as a by-product.* |
| `assert on` | kiểm chứng | *Assert on what appears on screen.* |

